## Workflow Preferences
- [Avoid explicit back-references to prior sections](feedback-no-explicit-back-references.md) — User dislikes "§1.1 has already developed/established..." stylistic phrasing; rewrite such instances unless absolutely necessary, just reiterate the point with parenthetical citation
- [No "supplies the canonical anchor" pattern](feedback-no-supplies-anchor-pattern.md) — Meta-narrative announcing source's function ("supplies the canonical scholarly anchor for X reading") forbidden; just state what source says + how it supports the claim. Flagged 2026-05-24 §1.3 L63 B1.1.
- [Greek faculty-names in user prose](feedback-greek-faculty-names.md) — Use *aisthētikon*, *orektikon*, *kritikon*, *kinētikon* etc. instead of English "faculty of X" formulations in user prose (quoted material preserves translator's English)
- [Backup before changes](feedback-backup-before-changes.md) — Always create timestamped `.backups/` before multi-file edits
- [Major iterations on copies](feedback-major-iterations-on-copies.md) — For major design iterations, work on copies in dedicated `*-iterations/` folders so originals stay as v0 baselines for A/B comparison
- [Per-paragraph revision protocol](feedback-per-paragraph-revision-protocol.md) — User-first 10-step collaboration for long-form writing revision (user edits → assistant TODO scan → approval → Q-response → implement)
- [Copy/paste line-break issue](feedback-copy-paste-line-breaks.md) — Long single-line LaTeX deliverables in chat code blocks pick up spurious newlines on paste; write to tmp file or apply Edit directly instead
- [Coined-compound restraint](feedback-coined-compound-restraint.md) — Avoid `\textit{long-hyphenated-coined-phrase}` labels in prose; prefer descriptive noun phrases with parenthetical glosses (single Greek/Latin terms in italics still fine)
- [Gross advisor-rigor for citations](feedback-gross-advisor-citation-rigor.md) — **UTMOST PRIORITY**: Daniel Gross is the dissertation advisor; ANY use of *Uncomfortable Situations* (2017) or *Heidegger and Rhetoric* (2005, ed. Gross) must be perfectly verbatim AND contextually accurate. Read full chapters as needed. Tracked as Task #18.
- [Plan review process](feedback-plan-review-process.md) — Multi-round review with external analysis, save to `plans/` folder
- [Max effort on gold-set annotations](feedback-annotation-max-effort.md) — Engage maximum reasoning per claim; no batch-shortcuts on load-bearing labels
- [corpus/index FIRST, ChromaDB fallback](feedback-corpus-index-first.md) — For scholarly source retrieval, consult corpus/index/ for locus identification before any ChromaDB query
- [Missing-source quotation placeholder](feedback-missing-source-placeholder.md) — When a required quote's source isn't in corpus, cite by Bekker/SZ/BCAP locus and use ****** as quotation body; user adds verbatim manually
- [Relaxed placeholder rule for citation marathon](feedback-missing-source-placeholder-relaxed.md) — During citation marathon ONLY: assistant may attempt WebSearch-sourced fill with `****** UNVERIFIED:` prefix as audit flag; never from training data alone; full audit footnote required
- [Verify Perplexity verbatims against PDFs](feedback-perplexity-verbatim-verification.md) — Perplexity verbatims + page-loci can be fabricated/wrong; cross-check against local PDFs in `corpus/rhetorical_ontology/`. UNVERIFIED prefix necessary not optional. Corpus/index page locations also need verification

